course: dictionary
lesson: 12684
title: Disused and forgotten
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disused is built from two parts. Dis- means not, and used means used. So disused means not used any more. You can see the clue in the word itself.
explain: A disused building is one that nobody uses now. «The children explored a disused railway tunnel.» The clues are explored and tunnel: they went inside, and a railway tunnel is one a train no longer uses. Disused means it is empty and left alone.
explain: Disused can also mean left empty and forgotten. «An old shop stood disused on the corner for ten years.» Nobody worked there or shopped there for a long time. When you meet disused, ask: has anyone used this for a long time? If not, it is probably disused.
fact: Disused means no longer used.
fact: «Disused» is often used for buildings, railways and mines: a disused factory, a disused mine.
fact: A disused place is often left empty and forgotten.
fact: Safety rule: keep out of disused quarries, wells and buildings, because they can be dangerous.
exercise: «The children found a disused railway line in the woods.» What does disused mean? | *Not used any more | Full of people every day | Very noisy with lots of trains | Brand new and shiny
exercise: Which of these is a disused building? | A shop open every day of the week | A new house still being built | A school with three hundred pupils | *A factory that has been empty for years
exercise: The sign says «Keep out of disused wells.» Why? | Nobody can see them | They are full of sweets | They are the best places to play | *They may be dangerous
test: «The old mine has been disused since the 1950s.» What does disused tell you about the mine? | It is busy every day with miners | It is famous for its gold | *It is no longer worked | It has just been opened
test: Jayden says, «A disused station is just a station that's broken.» What is the better meaning? | A station that is painted red | *A station that is no longer used | A station where people sing | A station that is very fast
exam: Read this: «The field held a disused barn, its door hanging off and its roof full of holes.» What does disused mean here? | Full of hay for the animals | *Left empty and no longer used | Used every single day by the farmer | Freshly painted for a party
